<p>As we can see, the outward expansion from the initially infected cell is=
 similar to how level-order traversal works in a tree, where each level rep=
resents nodes that are at a specific distance from the initially infected n=
ode.</p>
<p>So, let=E2=80=99s perform a level-order traversal to infect cells, start=
ing at the infected cell. <strong>Each level that gets traversed correspond=
s to 1-second passing in the infection process</strong>.</p>
